sentences.l:
Indeed is-safe the-eye-effaced from a-pit, * and-falls in-it the-seeing, the-gazing;
and-is-safe the-ignorant from a-slip, * and-perishes in-it the-learned, the-skilled;
and-is-in-difficulty the-believer in his-provision, * and-is-provided-for the-unbeliever and-the-wicked;
what (is) the-stratagem-of the-man and-what his-doing? * This (is) that-which decreed-it the-Able.

sentences.i:
The blind man may be spared the pit, while the one who sees and gazes falls into it;
the ignorant may be spared the slip, while the learned and skilled perish by it;
the believer is straitened in his living, while the unbeliever and the wicked are provided for.
What is a man's cunning, and what is his doing? This is what the Able has decreed.
